<<<
littoral, n., has a technical sense in which it is doubtless of value; marine life being distributed into abyssal, pelagic, & littoral, the l. (sc. zone or region) is the shallow waters near the shore.
===
**littoral, n.,** has a technical sense in which it is doubtless of value; marine life being distributed into abyssal, pelagic, & littoral, *the l.* (sc. zone or region) is the shallow waters near the shore.
>>>

<<<
should never be preferred to coast, & its present popularity is due to pretentiousness. Why not coast in The towns along the Mediterranean littoral, The Russian settlements on the Eastern Caspian littoral? See FORMAL WORDS.
===
should never be preferred to *coast,* & its present popularity is due to pretentiousness. Why not *coast* in *The towns along the Mediterranean littoral, The Russian settlements on the Eastern Caspian littoral?* See ^^FORMAL WORDS^^.
>>>

